What comes from upstream
------------------------
The application framework Coderax is built on originates in LibreChat,
including the API/client workspace layout, the conversation and message data
model, the prompt and agent infrastructure, and the localisation tooling.
Coderax adds product-layer work on top of that framework.

Runtime dependencies
--------------------
Coderax depends on packages published by the LibreChat project, including
@librechat/agents, installed from the npm registry under their own license
terms. Those packages are not vendored into this repository.

Maintaining upstream parity
---------------------------
The exact upstream commit this fork descends from is not recorded in this
repository. Recording that commit and its date here is recommended, so that
upstream security fixes can be rebased deliberately rather than by guesswork.

Reporting
---------
Security issues in upstream components should be reported to the LibreChat
project as well as to Coderax, where the issue is not specific to Coderax.
